dilemma where the other copy runs the same function on a different input. Intervening on my own policy doesn't move the other copy's action, since that's fixed by its own input, unless the grader treats the two as dependent. I'm checking the payoffs next, starting with the essay's self-coordination example.\n\nI'm working out what happens if the other copy's input is different: intervening on my policy alone leaves its action unchanged, so defection dominates under the essay's Equation 4. Policy-selection would cooperate, but the essay only offers that as an extension. I'm weighing whether the differing inputs might be logically linked anyway, and I'm leaning toward treating them as separate nodes, so I'll submit.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Working under A-FDT, I'm looking at a twin prisoner's dilemma where the other copy runs the same function on a different input. Intervening on my own policy doesn't move the other copy's action, since that's fixed by its own input, unless the grader treats the two as dependent. I'm checking the payoffs next, starting with the essay's self-coordination example.\n\nI'm working out what happens if the other copy's input is different: intervening on my policy alone leaves its action unchanged, so defection dominates under the essay's Equation 4. Policy-selection would cooperate, but the essay only offers that as an extension. I'm weighing whether the differing inputs might be logically linked anyway, and I'm leaning toward treating them as separate nodes, so I'll submit.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10081,"completion_tokens":1131,"total_tokens":11212,"cost":0.062944,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.062944,"upstream_inference_promp